Forgejo API fixtures (tests/forge.test.sh, tests/solo.test.sh, tests/run-cmd.test.sh,
tests/solo-visibility.test.sh), served by tests/lib/forgejo-stub.sh.

RECORDED answers were taken GET-only from the live server (Forgejo 17.0.1,
gitea-1.22.0, http://forgejo.internal) through lib/forge.sh's own request
helper (_forge_fj), so the token never left Celestial's code. Every recorded
file is anonymised: owner/repo become geoff/gizmo, product names in any string
become gizmo/Gizmo, emails are empty, avatar urls are /avatars/1, repository
descriptions and original (mirror) urls are empty, runner/task UUIDs and the
workflow network hash are zeroes, a run's event_payload is "{}", and PR, run
and review titles and bodies are neutral text. Where a test needs a scenario
the live server has no example of (a protected base, a stale approval, a
second reviewer), the RECORDED SHAPE is kept and only the named scenario
fields are overlaid on it.

